dist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repo is PUBLIC. Real client and internal documents must never enter it.
#
# Test material lives OUTSIDE the repo, at ~/RCDev/.tanka-testdata/. That is
# the primary control. Everything below is a backstop against a stray
# `git add -A`, because the drop zone and the repo sit next to each other and
# the first version of this file only covered Office formats. Client-named
# HTML and a zip landed in examples/ untracked-but-not-ignored, one command
# away from being published.
#
# examples/ is now deny-by-default: anything dropped there is ignored unless
# it is explicitly named below. Add a new synthetic example by adding its
# filename here, deliberately.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

examples/*
!examples/.gitkeep
!examples/README.md
!examples/before-status-report.md
!examples/after-status-report.md

# Document formats, anywhere in the tree
*.pdf
*.doc
*.docx
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.ppt
*.pptx
*.msg
*.eml
*.html
*.htm
*.csv
*.zip
